# The repo's canonical text form is LF, enforced at checkout too: no smudge
# boundary between working tree and repo.  Windows hosts run with
# core.autocrlf=true by default, which would otherwise materialise the
# Build Kit shell scripts as CRLF and break them on Linux/Android
# ("bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M").
# If a file class ever genuinely needs CRLF in the working tree (.bat/.cmd
# for cmd.exe), add a `*.bat text eol=crlf` override AFTER this line — the
# in-repo form stays LF; CRLF becomes checkout-time presentation only.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never normalised.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip binary
*.exe binary
